  "before": "before/native contains actual Compatibility captures of the old racing destination with Create challenge, Created and Share. Its existing graphical discovery suite passed80 checks before the new requirements were added.",
  "retained_initial_failure": {
    "log": "logs/TestScript-12316.log",
    "result": "CHALLENGE TAB: 60 checks, 1 failures",
    "cause": "The first loading-state assertion still expected the previous corrupted/legacy ellipsis literal. The UI and assertion now use the same proper Unicode Finding challenges ellipsis; the honest loading-state assertion remains."
  },
  "corrections": [
    "Initial native review exposed a cropped standings header; Race details and complete Standings now occupy separate tabs with shared pinned racing actions.",
    "A PowerShell-to-Python source-edit pipe converted a few newly introduced Unicode characters to question marks. All affected UI/test captions were corrected with UTF-8 patches before final captures.",
    "TabContainer owns its tab theme items; styling its internal TabBar was replaced with documented TabContainer overrides.",
    "The full selected-track outline was retained; only gallery thumbnails use the pre-existing bounded96-sample presentation.",
    "The integrated-test before copy was reconstructed by removing only its three new standings-tab activation lines; the other modified existing source before copies were captured before edits.",
    "Expanded-filter captures initially sampled the previous rendered frame. The native capture helper now settles layout and waits for frame completion after visibility changes; final Compatibility and Mobile110 checks pass with filters visible in the saved images. The empty-state icon uses the existing high-resolution vector rasterization."
  ],
  "reference_review": "https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_tabcontainer.html (native theme property ownership only)",
  "assets": "All three format illustrations and both distinct entry illustrations retain their exact recorded SHA-256 hashes.",
